# 075.RNAHairpin -- the bonded model on A-form RNA

A 12-nucleotide RNA hairpin (GGGCGCAAGCCU, GCAA tetraloop) under the same
model as 074.DNADuplex, from a SOLUTION NMR structure.

    make prep     build rna.nc
    make point    the energy table below
    make run      dynamics


## Why RNA is not just DNA with one more oxygen

Two things exist here that no DNA file has, and neither had ever been
exercised before this example:

  * the 2'-OH group, whose rotation is a real torsion of its own (it lands in
    the NUCLEIC_CHI family alongside the glycosidic bond);
  * the A-form geometry. RNA's sugars sit at C3'-endo where B-DNA's sit at
    C2'-endo, and that single difference is what makes the helix compact
    rather than wide.

Point energy at the input conformation:

    stretch      485.83 kJ/mol
    bend         713.79 kJ/mol
    dihedral     599.24 kJ/mol

against AMBER's 547.3 kJ/mol of torsion on the same axes: +8.9% over 132
axes. Per-axis torque correlation against AMBER: zeta 0.990, alpha 0.982,
chi 0.978 (the 12 glycosidic torsions AND the 12 2'-OH rotors), beta 0.901,
epsilon 0.868, gamma 0.853.


## The pucker test, which is the point of this example

The 12 sugars of 1ZIH enter at 100% C3'-endo, phase 12.9 degrees -- a clean
A-form signature, which is what makes this hairpin a test and not merely a
second nucleic structure. After 6 ps:

    amplitude   37.0 -> 31.1 degrees
    C3'-endo (North)   100% -> 100%, phase 12.9 -> 15.0 degrees

Every sugar keeps its state and its phase. The sugar ring carries no bonded
rule of its own and is held rigid by the mesh (see 074.DNADuplex's README for
why, and for the --stiffness/timestep coupling that follows from it), so this
shows the A-form is preserved -- not that the model would find it on its own
from a wrong starting point.


## Provenance

PDB 1ZIH, model 1: solution NMR, never a crystal. Standard residues only,
hydrogens rebuilt from the OL3 templates, energy minimised, then 50 ps of
Langevin dynamics at 300 K with GBn2 implicit solvent. A deposited structure
is restraint-derived and does not sit at the force field's own equilibrium;
the implicit solvent is not optional either, every phosphate carrying -1.


## What this cannot show

Same three limits as 074.DNADuplex: no IMPALA or hydrophobicity parameters,
terminal residues approximate to about 0.25 e, and the pucker preserved
rather than predicted.
